= Availability heuristic — Simple =

The '''availability heuristic''' is judging how common or likely something is by how easily examples come to mind.

If you recently heard several dramatic stories about airplane accidents, flying may feel more dangerous even if the actual risk has not changed much.

This shortcut can work when easy-to-remember events really are common.

It can mislead when vivid, emotional, unusual, or heavily reported events are easier to remember than ordinary events.

Availability is not just recency. Something old can still be very easy to remember.

